    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_c6ccc98e",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: obedience_meme; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The meme uses a photo of Kevin Hart, a Black comedian, in a context that appears to be a press conference or interview, with the overlaid text 'obedience' and a derogatory caption about people who don't smile being 'due to their constant painful hip they all seem to grasp.' This text is a harmful stereotype that links physical disability (specifically hip pain) to a perceived lack of emotional expression or social conformity, and implies that such individuals are 'obedient' or passive. The meme maps the image of a public figure (Kevin Hart) onto a negative, potentially mocking narrative about people with physical disabilities, which can be seen as ableist and degrading. The intent is to ridicule or belittle individuals with physical disabilities by associating their condition with a lack of social engagement or 'obedience,' which is a harmful and potentially offensive message.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_b0a2614e"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
